nd of a new center  after we view the old district rolander  shows me vilnius's modern side the  contemporary art center is the largest  in the baltics  it stages numerous exhibitions with  artists from around the world  it also has a very popular cinema we  watch our report from 2009  back then vilnius was proud to be a  european cultural capital  then the economic crisis struck and the  arts budget for the year was halved  the original director quit and verlander  stepped into the breach to salvage what  he could he managed to stage a range of  festivals and shows despite the tight  budget  the aim was to broaden the spectrum of  cultural events and facilities in  vilnius  so four years after  being the the cultural capital  would you say it helped the city to to  improve i think a lot of initiatives  which were born  preparing to become a culture capital  during the capital year  uh  survived this  this crisis times while the  the creative competition  but those initiatives aren't all that's  new and vilnius rolandis also shows us  an outlet of an extremely successful  fashion label julia janus  it now also sells designer household  objects like these candles the perfect  souvenir for the next euromax contest  we conclude our tour in bistro 18.  rolandis's favorite restaurant in the  old city  he hopes more places like it will open  because attractive shops and restaurants  help to draw more tourists after all he  says vilnius is far too beautiful to be  ignored
 

